  Material Symbols `visibility` (Outlined, weight 400, 24px), Apache License 2.0.
  Shown while the password is readable, the Material password-toggle convention:
  the open eye is the state, and the control's description names the action.

  No frame draws this control; it is an owner-approved addition. The fill is a
  token so the glyph follows the theme, as the input's placeholder does.

  **Drawn at 20dp, not the source's 24.** Material Symbols use the whole of their
  960 viewport - this glyph inks 22 of a 24dp box, 92% - while the Settings rows
  beside it carry legacy 24-viewport icons that ink 18, 75%. At equal box sizes
  the eye therefore read a fifth wider than every other icon in the app. 20dp
  brings its ink to 18.3 and matches them.

  This is the glyph only. `auth_password_toggle` is a 48dp ImageButton with
  scaleType=center, so the drawable is drawn at its intrinsic size inside an
  unchanged box: the touch target stays 48x48, the padding, the alignment and the
  contentDescription are untouched, and AuthLayoutTest still pins all of them.
-->
